	title 'Tool Locator Patch'********************************************************************* Copyright 1990-1992 Apple Computer, Inc.* All Rights Reserved********************************************************************** Tool Locator patches for ROM 3* * (Some routines are also used by the ROM 1 patch.)*** 17-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** New file for 6.0.** 25-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Added GetIndMessage call.** 3..4-Oct-90	Dave Lyons** Implemented AcceptRequests and most of SendRequest.** 10-Oct-90	Dave Lyons** Finish SendRequest (implement by-name substring matching).** 16-Oct-90	Dave Lyons** Add a NotifyProc to call SysBeep2 (AddTBNotifyProc).** 14-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Removed the JSL AddTBNotifyProc from TLBootInit (moving it to* Install.asm instead).** Put back all.macros.** 17-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Patched out StartUpTools and ShutDownTools.* Patched out LoadOneTool and LoadTools for new version* number bit handling.** 14-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Forced a device scan through the new $01FCDC vector before* adding the SysBeep2-calling NotifyProc; this way having a disk* online during boot doesn't cause a SysBeep2 "insert" call.** 22-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Changed the notify proc for insert/eject to check the DIB* of the device & see if it's a 5.25 drive.  If it is, we don't* call SysBeep2, because bogus inserts and ejects happen frequently* for these drives.** 29-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Only call SysBeep2 for inserts/ejects on devices that have* removable media!  (Brilliant...thanks, Greg.)** 16-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Added AddTBRequestHandler and UnknownDiskReqProc to this* file.  This IDs unrecognized disks within HandleDiskInsert* in the Window Manager.** 18-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Changed the request number in UnknownDiskReqProc to $0002,* systemSaysUnknownDisk.** 23-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Edited the unknown-disk messages to contain actual installer* script names.** 30-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Unknown disk messages:  Changed "seems" to "appears" in all* messages.  Changed "use" to "read" in ISO/HS message.** 23-May-91	Dave Lyons** Added a missing REP #$30 that would cause a tool call to be* made in 8-bit accumulator, which is normally fine, but was* accidental and caused a crash with old versions of GSBug.** 6-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Patched TLShutDown to call SANEShutDown first thing.** Patched Save/RestoreTextState to deal with text page 1* shadowing.  RestoreTextState(NIL) now does nothing.** 11-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** Optimized stack setup and teardown on AcceptRequests.** 1-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** SendRequest now returns error $0122, invalidSendRequest, if* you try to send a $8000+ request by sendToAll.** 8-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** The UnknownDisk request proc now accepts systemSaysDeskShutDown* and systemSaysDeskStartUp.  On startup, it calls ShowBootInfo* with StringPtr=$80000000 to reinitialize it.  On the first* shutdown, it calls SysBeep2(sbSystemStartup+sbSilence).** 14-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Made TLShutDown call QDAuxShutDown for some BONEHEADS who* are making ShutDownTools shut down the tool locator, and* *then* they are shutting down QuickDraw, which would have* shut down QDAux for them, but it's already gone.  (They* never asked for QDAux in the first place, but Window Mgr* loaded it so AlertWindow could use icons.)** 17-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Moved following functions to Tool.Setup instead of here:*  LoadTools, LoadOneTool, UnloadOneTool, StartUpTools,*  ShutDownTools, GetMsgHandle, AcceptRequests, SendRequest.*  Also moved TBNotifyProc and AddTBRequestHandler/UnknownDiskProc.** 18-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Added a placeholder proc to be linked into the very beginning* of the Patches segment of Tool.Setup, so that no tool patch* will start at the beginning of the segment, and therefore at* the beginning of the bank (can't be dispatched to correctly).** 23-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** SendRequest, on dispatch to a request proc, sets D to $CCCC* and Bank to $FE, to help catch request procs that mistakenly* assume the B or D values are defined or useful.  They are not.** 1-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** Changed MS-DOS unrecognized-disk message.** 13-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** AcceptRequests--if NamePtr and ReqProc are both NIL, we remove* all the procs registered under the specified UserID.** 24-Oct-91	Dave Lyons** UnknownDisk proc can identify UniDOS (DOS 3.3 on floppy) disks* (reads block $0110 instead of $0088 looking for the VTOC).** 2-Dec-91	Dave Lyons (for 6.0d60)** Hack MessageCenter so that deleting message 1 (list of Pascal* strings to Open/Print, from Finder) automatically deletes* message $11 (new mesage, list of GS/OS strings to Open/Print* from Finder). -- This is needed so that a new app doesn't* accidentally act on message $11 after transferring out of* an old application that didn't know about the new message.** 27-Jan-92	Dave Lyons (for 6.0d66)** SendRequest was failing to fill in the recvCount field of* the output buffer, in the case that the stop-after-one flag* is set and somebody accepts the request.  Fixed.** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Version $0301 for 6.0 final (linked into both TS2 and TS3).********************************************************************* 17-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Version $8302 for 6.0.1d1.** Changed 6.0 to 6.1 in a couple of you-have-no-FST messaages.** 9-Jun-92	Dave Lyons** UnknownDisk procedure:  Updated some messages to read 6.0.1* instead of 6.1.  Updated MS-DOS message to tell them to install* the MS-DOS FST using the Installer.** 18-Jan-93	Steve Stephenson** Optimized IsThisTarget, mcGetFirstMessage, and mcGetNextMessage* for speed (also shrunk them in size).** 2-Apr-93 DAL** Version $0302 for 6.0.1.*************************************************************************************************************************************	include 'all.macros'	include ':::sys.equs.asm'incbusy	equ $e10064MessNotFound	equ $0111	;error codesrqNameTooLong	equ $0113	;for AcceptRequestsreqNotAccepted	equ $0120	;SendRequest error codeduplicateName	equ $0121	;AcceptRequests duplicate stringinvalidSendRequest	equ $0122	;can't send $8000+ to everybodyLocatorVersion	equ $0302	;2-Apr-93 DAL****************************************************************** GODDAMMIT, I need to put a NOP at the beginning of the* Patches segment to prevent a tool patch from starting at the* first byte of the segment & maybe the bank, where you can't* dispatch to it.*****************************************************************GODDAMMIT	PROC EXPORT	nop	Endp****************************************************************** TLTable** This is the Function pointer Table (FPT) for the tool* locator tool set.** Note:  Functions marked with "[ts]" are already patched for*        us in Tool.Setup.*****************************************************************LocatorCallTable	proc EXPORT	IMPORT TLBootInit	IMPORT TLVersion;	import AcceptRequests	;17-Sep-90 DAL;	import SendRequest		;17-Sep-90 DAL;	import GetMsgHandle		;25-Sep-90 DAL;	import StartUpTools		;17-Nov-90 DAL;	import ShutDownTools	;17-Nov-90 DAL;	import LoadOneTool		;17-Nov-90 DAL;	import LoadTools		;17-Nov-90 DAL;	import UnloadOneTool	;25-Nov-90 DAL	import TLShutDown		;6-Jun-91 DAL	import SaveTextState	;6-Jun-91 DAL	import RestoreTextState	;6-Jun-91 DAL	import MessageCenter	;2-Dec-91 DALTheBeginning	dc.L (TheEnd-TheBeginning)/4	; call count + 1	dc.L TLBootInit-1		; TLBootInit (0101)	dc.L 0		; TLStartUp  (0201)	dc.L TLShutDown-1		; TLShutDwon (0301)	dc.L TLVersion-1		; TLVersion  (0401)	dc.L 0		; TLReset    (0501)	dc.L 0		; TLStatus   (0601)	dc.L 0		; NotImp     (0701)	dc.L 0		; NotImp     (0801)	dc.L 0		; GetTSPtr   (0901)	dc.L 0		; SetTSPtr   (0A01)	dc.L 0		; GetFuncPtr (0B01)	dc.L 0		; GetWAP     (0C01)	dc.L 0		; SetWAP     (0D01)	dc.L 0	;[ts] LoadTools-1	; 0e01	dc.L 0	;[ts] LoadOneTool-1	   ; 0f01	dc.L 0	;[ts] UnloadOneTool-1  ; 1001	dc.L 0 		; TLMountVolume     1101	dc.L 0 		; TLTextMountVolume 1201	dc.L SaveTextState-1 	; SaveTextState     1301	dc.L RestoreTextState-1	; RestoreTextState  1401	dc.L MessageCenter-1	; MessageCenter     1501 patched 2-Dec-91 DAL	dc.L 0 		; SetDefaultTPT     1601	dc.L 0 		; MessageByName     1701	dc.L 0	;[ts] StartupTools-1    ; StartUpTools      1801	dc.L 0	;[ts] ShutDownTools-1   ; ShutDownTools     1901*** New calls for 6.0	dc.l 0	;[ts] GetMsgHandle-1    ; 1A01  17-Sep-90 DAL	dc.l 0	;[ts] AcceptRequests-1  ; 1B01  17-Sep-90 DAL	dc.l 0	;[ts] SendRequest-1	    ; 1C01  17-Sep-90 DALTheEnd	EndP****************************************************************** ROM 3 patch for TLVersion*****************************************************************TLVersion	proc export	export TLBootInit	lda #LocatorVersion	sta 7,s** This null routine is called when the patch is installed.* it should never be called again.*TLBootInit	oEndCall0	lda #0	clc	rtl	EndP****************************************************************** SaveTextState -- new patch 6-Jun-91 DAL** Call the ROM 3 SaveTextState code, and then stuff the text* shadow bit into bit 0 of offset 1 in the resulting record,* and enable text shadowing.*****************************************************************SaveTextState	proc	pha	pha	jsl ToROM	tax	;keep error code	lda 3,s	sta 9+4,s	lda 1,s	sta 7+4,s	lda 2,s	beq @exit	phx	;save error	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [5],y	tax	lda [5]	sta 5	stx 7	;dereferenced result	lda >$e0c035	lsr a	;text state in Carry	php	ldy #1	lda [5],y	;get old value from record, strip bit 0	lsr a	plp	;get text state back in Carry	rol a	;put text state into bit 0	sta [5],y	pld	plx	;restore error code@exit	pla	pla	;pop my temp result space	lda >$e0c035	lsr a	asl a	;clear bit 0 = enable text shadowing	sta >$e0c035	txa	cmp #1	rtlToROM	jsl $fdc8d6	rtl	EndP****************************************************************** RestoreTextState -- new patch 6-Jun-91 DAL** Check for a NIL state handle; do nothing if NIL.** Set text shadowing bit from bit 0 of offset 1 in the state* handle.*****************************************************************RestoreTextState	proc	lda 8,s	;check middle word of handle	beq @nil	phd	lda 11,s	pha	lda 11,s	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	sta 1	stx 3	dey	;Y=1 = offset into state record	lda [1],y	lsr a	;text state in Carry	php	lda >$e0c035	lsr a	plp	;text state back in Carry	rol a	sta >$e0c035	pla	pla	pld	jml >$fdca4c	;RestoreTextState in ROM@nil	ldx #0	ldy #4	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	EndP****************************************************************** MessageCenter -- new patch 2-Dec-91 DAL** When deleting message 1, also automatically delete message $0011.*****************************************************************MessageCenter	procsTheHandle	equ 7	;offsets into stacksTheType	equ sTheHandle+4sTheAction	equ sTheType+2	lda sTheAction,s	cmp #3	;delete	bne @notKludge	lda sTheType,s	dec a	bne @notKludge	pea 3	;action=delete	pea $0011	;message = new Types msg	phx	phx	;handle = ignored	_MessageCenter@notKludge	jml >$fdc13e	;MessageCenter in ROM 3*** end 2-Dec-91****************************************************************** TLShutDown -- new patch 6-Jun-91 DAL** In case the stoopid application left SANE started up, we'll* shut it down for them.  This avoids, say, an NDA seeing that* SANE is still started & using it, when it's actually using* some memory that is no longer allocated (ouch!).*****************************************************************TLShutDown	proc export	_QDAuxShutDown	;added 14-Sep-91 DAL	_SANEShutDown	jml >$fe0342	;original ROM 3 TLShutDown	EndP****************************************************************** GetMsgHandle for both ROM 1 and ROM 3** $1A01 GetMsgHandle(Flags,MsgRef/4):Handle** Inputs:**     WORD Flags = %0000 0000 0000 00mm*        mm 00 = get the MsgRef-th message*        mm 01 = get message with Message Type of MsgRef*        mm 10 = get message with name MsgRef points to*        mm 11 = reserved**     LONG MsgRef:*        index or integer or pointer to Pascal string (depends on Flags)** Outputs:*     LONG Handle = handle belonging to the system (don't fiddle with it!)*                   (NIL if error)** Description:*****************************************************************GetMsgHandle	proc export	import mcGetFirstMessage	import mcGetNextMessage	import DerefYA	DefineStacktemp	longsizeLocals	EndLocalssaveDPage	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3MsgRef	longFlags	wordResultHandle	long	jsl incbusy	phd	tsc	sec	sbc #sizeLocals	tcs	tcd	jsr mcGetFirstMessage	bcs @notFound@next	sty <ResultHandle+2	sta <ResultHandle	jsr CheckMessage	ldx #0	;anticipate success	bcc @exit	ldy <ResultHandle+2	lda <ResultHandle	jsr mcGetNextMessage	bcc @next@notFound	ldx #MessNotFound	stz <ResultHandle+2	stz <ResultHandle@exit	tsc	;get rid of local variables	clc	adc #sizeLocals	tcs	pld	ldy #6	;strip 6 bytes	jml ToBusyStrip** CheckMessage** Inputs:  YA = handle to a message to check*               (also in ResultHandle)*          Flags and MsgRef tell us what to check** Outputs:*          CLC if we found the message*CheckMessage	jsr DerefYA	sty <temp+2	sta <temp	lda <flags	and #%00000011	asl a	tax	jmp (Filter,x)Filter	dc.w byIndex,byType,byName,byReservedbyIndex	dec <MsgRef	clc	beq @found	sec@found	rtsbyType	ldy #4	;offset to type	lda [<temp],y	cmp <MsgRef	clc	beq @found	sec@found	rts** byName--return CLC if message at <temp was created by*         MessageByName and the name matches <MsgRef*byName	ldy #4	;offset to type	lda [<temp],y	bpl @noMatch	;$8000+ = MessageByName types	cmp #$b0b0	;Claris stole Msg Type $B0B0	beq @noMatch	clc	lda <temp	adc #8	sta <temp	bcc @ok	inc <temp+2@ok	sep #$30	longa off	longi off	lda [<MsgRef]	tay@compare	lda [<MsgRef],y	cmp [<temp],y	bne @cmpFail	dey	bpl @compare	longa on	longi on	rep #$30	clc	rts@cmpFail	rep #$30	longa on	longi on	;fall into sec/rts@noMatchbyReserved	sec	rts	EndP********************************************************************** Get YA=handle to first message (return SEC = none)** The handle to the first message is stored in the* Memory Manager's WAP.*****************************************************************mcGetFirstMessage	proc export;	pha;	pha	;result space (long);	pea 0	;system tool;	pea 2	;memory manager;	_GetWAP;	pla;	ply;	bne @ok;	sec;@ok	rts*** optimized 18-Jan-93 SS	import DerefYA	lda >$e103c8+2	tay	lda >$e103c8	;get ptr to WAPT	clc	adc #2*4	;get Memory Mgr's WAP	bcc @nohi	iny@nohi	jsr DerefYA	;dig out the handle	rts	*** end 18-Jan-93		EndP	** Advance YA to next message (return SEC = none)*mcGetNextMessage	proc export	jsr DerefYA	bcc DerefYA	rts	*** optimized 15-Jan-93 SS	export DerefYA;DerefYA	phd;	phy;	pha;	tsc;	tcd;	ldy #2;	lda [1],y;	pha;	lda [1];	ply	;conditions Z for bne;	clc;	bne @notNIL;	sec;@notNIL	plx;	plx;	pld;	rtsDerefYA	phb	;save B	phy	;reset to Y bnk	plb	;(invalid byte still on stk)	tax	;addr lo	lda |0,x	ldy |2,x	;hi=0=end	clc		bne @notNIL	sec@notNIL	plb	;pop garbage byte	plb	;restore B	rts	*** end 15-Jan-93	endp****************************************************************** AcceptRequests for both ROM 1 and ROM 3** $1B01 AcceptRequests(@NameStr,UserID,@ReqProc)** Description:** Uses MessageByName to create a message based on the* input parameters.  The name is $FF ">" followed by* the NameStr, and the UserID and ReqProc come after* that.** If ReqProc is NIL, removes the corresponding entry* instead.** Special case--if NamePtr and ReqProc are *both* NIL,* then we remove all the procs registered under the* specified UserID.*****************************************************************AcceptRequests	proc export	DefineStacksizeLocals	EndLocalssaveDPage	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3ReqProc	longUserID	wordNamePtr	long	jsl incbusy	phd	tsc	if sizeLocals<>0 then	sec	sbc #sizeLocals	tcs	endif	tcd	phb	phk	plb*** added 13-Oct-91 DAL -- allow removing procs by ID	lda <NamePtr+1	ora <ReqProc+1	bne @notRemoveByID	lda <UserID	jsr RemoveByUserID	ldx #0	brl @exit	;error code in X@notRemoveByID*** end 13-Oct-91	ldx #srqNameTooLong	;anticipate name too long	lda [NamePtr]	and #$00ff	cmp #63	bcs @exit	inc a	inc a	pha	;save length+2	sep #$20	sta msgString	rep #$20	tay	beq @copied@copy	lda [<NamePtr],y	sta msgString+2,y	dey	bne @copy@copied	ply	;length+2	lda <UserID	sta msgString+1,y	lda <ReqProc	sta msgString+1+2,y	lda <ReqProc+2	sta msgString+1+4,y	lda [<NamePtr]	and #$00ff	clc	adc #11	sta msgBuffer	lda <ReqProc+1	bne @Install*** Remove	ldy #0	;don't create	jsr MessByName	;return A=flag, Y=ID, X=error	pea 3	;delete message	phy	;message id	pha	pha	;handle (ignored)	_MessageCenter	tax	bra @exit*** Install@Install	ldy #0	;don't create msg	jsr MessByName	;return A=flag, Y=ID, X=error	ldx #duplicateName	;error	bcc @exit	;no error?  Duplicate name!	ldy #1	;okay to create msg	jsr MessByName	;return A=flag, Y=ID, X=error** X = error code@exit	plb	if sizeLocals<>0 then	tsc	;get rid of local variables	clc	adc #sizeLocals	tcs	endif	pld	ldy #10	;strip 10 bytes	jml ToBusyStrip*** added 13-Oct-91 DALRemoveByUserID	sta IDToRemove	phd	pha	pha	pha	pha	tsc	tcd@ThisMsg	equ 1@temp	equ 5@RestartTheSearch	jsr mcGetFirstMessage	bcs @removedByID@remove1	sty <@ThisMsg+2	sta <@ThisMsg	jsr DerefYA	sty <@temp+2	sta <@temp	ldy #4	lda [<@temp],y	;get message type	bpl @tryNext	;not a named message!	ldy #9	lda [<@temp],y	;check SendRequest signature	cmp #$3EFF	;$FF ">" signature	bne @tryNext	ldy #8	;offset to name length	lda [<@temp],y	and #$00FF	clc	adc #9	;offset past end of name (to user id)	tay	lda [<@temp],y	cmp IDToRemove	bne @tryNext	pea 3	;delete message	ldy #4	lda [<@temp],y	pha	;pushed message number (type)	pha	pha	;handle (not used)	_MessageCenter	bcs @removedByID	;shouldn't happen (give up)	bra @RestartTheSearch ;handle is invalid, start over@tryNext	ldy <@ThisMsg+2	lda <@ThisMsg	jsr mcGetNextMessage	bcc @remove1@removedByID	pla	pla	pla	pla	pld	rtsIDToRemove	dc.w 0*** end 13-Oct-91MessByName	pha	;space for result flag	pha	;space for result ID	phy	;CreateIt flag	pushlong #MsgBuffer	_MessageByName	tax	;error code	ply	;message ID created or found	pla	;Created flag	rtsmsgBuffer	dc.w 0	;length = [NameStr]+11msgString	dc.b 0	;length byte = [NameStr]+2	dc.b $ff,'>'	ds 63+2+4	endp****************************************************************** SendRequest for both ROM 1 and ROM 3** $1C01 SendRequest(ReqCode,How,Target/4,@In,@Out)** Inputs:** Outputs:** Description:*****************************************************************SendRequest	proc export	import mcGetFirstMessage	import mcGetNextMessage	DefineStackTempPtr	longtemp	longcount	wordsizeLocals	EndLocalssaveDPage	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3OutPtr	longInPtr	longTarget	longSendHow	wordReqCode	word	jsl incbusy	phd	tsc	sec	sbc #sizeLocals	tcs	tcd	stz <count*** added 1-Jul-91 DAL -- don't allow sendToAll + reqCode>=$8000	lda <reqCode	bpl @validSRQ	lda <sendHow	and #3	bne @validSRQ	ldx #invalidSendRequest	bra @exit@validSRQ*** end of 1-Jul-91 DAL	jsr mcGetFirstMessage	bcs @triedAll@next	sty <temp+2	sta <temp	jsr SendReq	bcs @doNext* request was accepted	inc <count	lda <SendHow	bmi @noError	;stop when it's accepted@doNext	ldy <temp+2	lda <temp	jsr mcGetNextMessage	bcc @next@triedAll;** If there's an output buffer, fill in the acceptedCount field;	lda <OutPtr+1;	beq @noOutBuff;	lda <count;	sta [<OutPtr];@noOutBuff	ldx #reqNotAccepted	;anticipate nobody accepted	lda <count	beq @exit@noError	ldx #0@exit*** moved here 27-Jan-92 DAL from above--set the recvCount in dataOut** If there's an output buffer, fill in the acceptedCount field	lda <OutPtr+1	beq @noOutBuff	lda <count	sta [<OutPtr]@noOutBuff*** end 27-Jan-92	tsc	;get rid of local variables	clc	adc #sizeLocals	tcs	pld	ldy #16	;strip 16 bytes	jml ToBusyStrip** SendReq** YA are a message handle.  Try sending the request to this if it's a* ReqProc message.** Return carry clear if the message is accepted.*SendReq	jsr DerefYA	sty <TempPtr+2	sta <TempPtr		ldy #4	lda [<TempPtr],y	bpl Noper	;not a $8000+ message type	ldy #9	lda [<TempPtr],y	cmp #$3eff	;$FF ">" signature	bne Noper	jsr IsThisTarget	bcs Noper1	;bypass redundant SEC (18-Jan-93 SS)	ldy #8	lda [<TempPtr],y	and #$00ff	clc	adc #12	;offset to proc+1	tay	lda [<TempPtr],y	tax	dey	lda [<TempPtr],y	phb	;save B around reqProc (23-Sep-91 DAL)	phd	;save D around reqProc (23-Sep-91 DAL)	pea 0	;result space	pei <ReqCode	pei <InPtr+2	pei <InPtr	pei <OutPtr+2	pei <OutPtr	jsl JumpToProc	pla	pld	;restore our D (23-Sep-91 DAL)	plb	;restore our B (23-Sep-91 DAL)	eor #$8000	asl a	rtsNoper	secNoper1	rts** IsThisTarget--return CLC if the message at <TempPtr is one* we should call.  We already know it's a ReqProc message.*IsThisTarget	lda <SendHow	and #%00000011	bne @notToAll@Yes	clc	;%00 = send to all	rts@notToAll	dec a	bne @notByName	;%01 = send by name substring* compare names: return CLC if Target is a substring of TempPtr+8 string* (TempPtr+8 pstring has $FF $3E as the first two characters; we ignore* them)	;	pei <TempPtr+2	;save old TempPtr;	pei <TempPtr;	clc;	lda <TempPtr;	adc #8	;offset to name;	sta <TempPtr;	bcc @1;	inc <TempPtr+2;@1;	longa off;	longi off;	sep #$30;	ldy #0;@nextChar	tya;	cmp [<Target];	bcs @decideYes	;run out of chars in Target: send;	inc a;	inc a;	cmp [<TempPtr];	dec a;	dec a;	bcs @decideNo	;run out of chars in candidate: don't send;	iny;	lda [<Target],y;	iny;	iny;	cmp [<TempPtr],y;	php;	dey;	dey;	plp;	beq @nextChar	;keep looking;;@decideNo	sec;	dc.b $24	;BIT <$xx hides next byte;@decideYes	clc;@decided	rep #$30;	longa on;	longi on;	pla;	sta <TempPtr;	pla;	sta <TempPtr+2;	rts	;Return value = carry*** optimized 18-Jan-93 SS	clc	;(for both adc and nil case)	lda [<Target]	and #$00ff	beq @defaultYes	;Target NIL is a match	adc #8+2+1	;length + offset to str + first 2 chars + 1 past	tay	;hold spot into TempPtr str where Target ends	ldx <Target	;set X for start of str	lda <Target+2	phb	;save B	pha	;reset to Target's B	plb	phy	longa off	sep #$20	ldy #8	lda [<TempPtr],y	;this Temp's length	dec a	;minus 2 for the lead chars	dec a	cmp |0,x	;long enuf to encompass the Target?	bcc @decideNo	; no, reject	iny	; yes, step to first actual char	iny	iny@nxtchar	lda [<TempPtr],y	;compare chars	cmp |1,x	bne @decideNo	;not same, reject	inx	iny	;bump indexes	tya	cmp 1,s	;at end of Target?	beq @decideYes	; yes, got a match	bcc @nxtchar	; not yet, keep checking@decideNo	sec	dc.b $90	;fake to skip over next byte@decideYes	clc	longa on	rep #$20	pla	;fix stack	plb	plb	;restore B@defaultYes	rts	*** end 18-Jan-93@notByName	dec a	bne @dontSend	;%10 = send by MemID* compare user IDs	ldy #8	;offset to string length	lda [<TempPtr],y	and #$00ff	clc	adc #9	;offset to User ID	tay	;added 20-Dec-90 DAL	lda [<TempPtr],y	cmp <Target	bne @DontSend	clc	rts@DontSend	sec	rts** JumpToProc--Long jump to address in XA*JumpToProc	phx	phb	;just a scratch byte	dec a	sta 1,s*** set up garbage values for undefined registers! (23-Sep-91 DAL)	lda #$CCCC	;garbage D value	tcd	pea $FEFE	plb	plb	;set B to $FE (ROM)*** end 23-Sep-91	rtl	EndP****************************************************************** AddTBNotifyProc for both ROM 1 and ROM 3** Description:** Adds a GS/OS Notify Proc that calls SysBeep2 in response* to various OS events.  This makes it easy to customize sounds* (or whatever) in the system.*****************************************************************AddTBNotifyProc	proc export*** Force a device scan so we get any "inserts" out of the way*** before we start calling SysBeep2 for every insert.  Having*** a disk online when you boot shouldn't count as an insert*** for SysBeep2 purposes. (14-Mar-91 DAL)*** 1-Apr-91 DAL -- use the Misc Tools call instead of the OS Service	pha	_ScanDevices	pla	_AddNotifyProcGS anpParms	rtlanpParms	dc.w 1	dc.l TBNotifyProc****************************************************************** TBNotifyProc -- call SysBeep2 as appropriate*****************************************************************TBNotifyProc	dc.l 0	;reserved	dc.w 0	;reserved	dc.w $A55A	dc.l $0000003E	;shutdown, eject, insert, OS switchesEventCode	dc.l 0ProcEntry* Need to check for eject/insert Apple 5.25 device--don't call SysBeep2	lda >EventCode	cmp #$0008	beq @isInsertEject	cmp #$0010	bne @notInsertEject@isInsertEject	phd	lda #$bd00	;hard-coded GS/OS direct page location	tcd	ldy #$0034	;offset of device_id in DIB	lda [$20],y	;$20 points to current DIB*** added 29-Mar-91 DAL	beq @willSkip; check for removable media now	ldy #$0008	;offset of characteristics in DIB	lda [$20],y	;$20 points to current DIB	and #$0004	;bit 2 set for removable media*** end of 29-Mar-91 DAL@willSkip	pld	tax	beq @skipit	;device_id $0000 is AppleDisk 5.25 drive@notInsertEject	lda >EventCode	ldx #$8010-1	;beepType = $8010 + bit number@findbit	inx	lsr a	bcc @findbit	phx	_SysBeep2@skipit	rtl	EndP********************************************************************************************************************************** AddTBRequestHandler -- install the toolbox's AcceptRequests*	     routine.*****************************************************************AddTBRequestHandler	proc export	import UnknownDiskReqProc	pushlong #myReqProcName	pha	_MMStartUp	pushlong #UnknownDiskReqProc	_AcceptRequests	rtlmyReqProcName	dc.b 18,'Apple~UnknownDisk~'	EndP**************************************************************** UnknownDiskReqProc** by Dave Lyons, 13-Apr-91** When this gets called, dataIn contains the device number* of a disk on which the Volume call returned error $52, or* possibly some other error that indicates no FST wanted to* claim the thing.** If we accept the request, we must put a return code at* [dataOut],4:  0=eject the thing, 1=initialize, 2=erase,* $ffff = leave the disk online and report no error.***************************************************************UnknownDiskReqProc	proc exportsystemSaysUnknownDisk equ $0002fsid_ProDOS	equ $0001fsid_DOS33	equ $0002fsid_DOS32	equ $0003fsid_Pascal	equ $0004fsid_MFS	equ $0005fsid_HFS	equ $0006fsid_Lisa	equ $0007fsid_CPM	equ $0008fsid_reserved	equ $0009fsid_MSDOS	equ $000afsid_HighSierra	equ $000bfsid_ISO9660	equ $000cfsid_AppleShare	equ $000dfakefsid_DOS33other	equ $000e	;not really a FSID (DOS 3.3 on unsupported device)sig_MFS	equ $D7D2	;block 2 signaturesig_HFS	equ $4442	;block 2 signaturebuffHandle	equ 1buffPtr	equ buffHandle+4oldDPage	equ buffPtr+4RTL1	equ oldDPage+2DataOut	equ RTL1+3DataIn	equ DataOut+4Request	equ DataIn+4Result	equ Request+2		phd	pha	pha	;space for buffPtr	pha	pha	;space for buffHandle	tsc	tcd		phb	phk	plb	stz <buffHandle+1	lda <Request*** 8-Jul-91 DAL -- handle systemSaysDeskStartUp and systemSaysDeskShutDown	cmp #$0502	;systemSaysDeskStartUp	bne @notDeskStart	pea $8000	lda #0	pha	;StringPtr = $80000000	pha	pha	;IconPtr = nil	_ShowBootInfo	;initialize ShowBootInfo!	bra @didIt@notDeskStart	cmp #$0503	;systemSaysDeskShutDown	bne @notDeskShut	lda >@FirstDeskShutDown	bne @didIt	inc a	sta >@FirstDeskShutDown	pea $8031	;sbSystemStartup+sbSilence	_SysBeep2@didIt	sec	ror <Result	bra @FastExit@FirstDeskShutDown	dc.w 0@notDeskShut*** end of 8-Jul-91	cmp #systemSaysUnknownDisk	bne @FastExit	lda <DataIn	beq @exit	jsr IdentifyTheDisk	;returns file system ID in A	tay	beq @exit	jsr CheckForFST	;input = A; output = unchanged or zero	tay	beq @exit	jsr AskWhatToDo	;returns SEC if [dataOut],4 is valid	ror <result@exit	lda <buffHandle+1	beq @fastExit	pei <buffHandle+2	pei <buffHandle	_DisposeHandle@FastExit	plb	pla	pla	;removed buffHandle	pla	pla	;removed buffPtr	pld	lda 2,s	sta 12,s	lda 1,s	sta 11,s	ply	ply	ply	ply	ply	rtl***************************************************************** IdentifyTheDisk** Input:  A = device number** Output: A = file system ID, 0 if unknown** Allocates buffHandle if necessary.  Caller will dispose.****************************************************************IdentifyTheDisk	sta rbDevNum	sta DInfoDevNum	pushlong #DInfoParms	pea $202c	;DInfo	jsl $e100b0	pha	pha	pea 0	pea $0200	;block size	pha	_MMStartUp	;memory ID	pea $c000	;attributes	pha	pha	_NewHandle	plx	ply	bcc @gotbuff	brl @unknown@gotbuff	sty <buffHandle+2	stx <buffHandle	ldy #2	lda [<buffHandle]	sta <buffPtr	sta rbAddress	lda [<buffHandle],y	sta <buffPtr+2	sta rbAddress+2	lda #2	sta rbBlockNum@tryAgain	pushlong #rbParms	pea $202f	jsl $e100b0	bcc @ok	cmp #$002e	;disk switched?	beq @tryAgain	bra @block2failed@ok	lda [buffPtr]	ldx #fsid_MFS	cmp #sig_MFS	beq @returnX	ldx #fsid_HFS	cmp #sig_HFS	beq @returnX; check for Pascal	jsr CheckForPascal	ldx #fsid_Pascal	bcc @returnX; check for ProDOS	jsr CheckForProDOS	ldx #fsid_ProDOS	bcc @returnX@block2failed; check for MS-DOS -- block 0 starts out $E9, or $EB $xx $90	stz rbBlockNum@zerotryAgain	pushlong #rbParms	pea $202f	jsl $e100b0	bcc @ZeroOK	cmp #$002e	;disk switched?	beq @zeroTryAgain	bra @block0failed@ZeroOk	lda [buffPtr]	and #$00ff	ldx #fsid_MSDOS	cmp #$00e9	beq @returnX	cmp #$00eb	bne @notMSDOS	ldy #2	lda [buffPtr],y	and #$00ff	cmp #$0090	beq @returnX@notMSDOS@block0failed; check for DOS 3.3 (return CLC for DOS 3.3)	jsr CheckForDOS33	bcs @not33	ldx #fsid_DOS33	lda DeviceID	beq @returnX	ldx #fakefsid_DOS33other	bra @returnX@not33; check for ISO/HighSierra	jsr CheckForISOandHS	bcc @returnX; unknown disk@unknown	ldx #0@returnX	txa	rts***************************************************************** CheckForDOS33** Input: copy of block 2 in [buffPtr]* Output: CLC if it's a DOS 3.3 disk (trashed buffer)****************************************************************CheckForDOS33	lda #17*8	;track 17, sector 0	jsr @CheckForDOSBlkA	bcs @tryUniDOS	rts@tryUniDOS	lda #17*16	;track 17, sector 0 for UniDOS@CheckForDOSBlkA	sta rbBlockNum@zerotryAgain	pushlong #rbParms	pea $202f	jsl $e100b0	bcs @notDOS33	sep #$30		;work with bytes	LONGI OFF	LONGA OFF	ldx #id_tbl_end-id_values-1	;point to last entry in id tables@loop1	lda id_offset,x		;get offset into VTOC	tay@loop2	lda [buffPtr],y		;get the actual value	cmp id_values,x		;compare to the table value	bne @false		;not the same@loop3	dex	bmi @confirmed		;table finished	tya	cmp id_offset,x		;skip over other entries for same position	beq @loop3	bra @loop1		;move on to next compare@false	dex	bmi @notDOS33	tya	cmp id_offset,x		;see if there's an alternate value for that offset	beq @loop2		;yes, get a second chance@notDOS33	rep #$30	sec	rts@confirmed	rep #$30	clc	rts	longa on	longi onid_offset		;these are offsets into the VTOC of bytes which are checked in order		;to determine whether a disk is DOS 3.3 format:	dc.b $3		;DOS release #	dc.b $27	;# of T/S pairs per T/S list sector	dc.b $36,$37	;# of bytes per sector	dc.b $31,$31	;direction of track allocation (2 possible values)	dc.b $34,$34	;# of tracks per disk (2 possible values??)	dc.b $35,$35	;# of sectors per track (2 possible values??)id_values		;these are the actual values required for a DOS 3.3 disk:	dc.b 3		;DOS release #	dc.b $7A	;# of T/S pairs per T/S list sector	dc.b $00,$01	;# of bytes per sector	dc.b $01,$FF	;direction of track allocation (2 possible values)	dc.b 35,50	;# of tracks per disk (2 possible values??)	dc.b 16,32	;# of sectors per track (2 possible values??)id_tbl_end***************************************************************** CheckForPascal** This is the id_block routine borrowed from the Pascal FST.** Input: copy of block 2 in [buffPtr]* Output: CLC if it's a Pascal disk****************************************************************io_file_count	equ $10		; offset to number of files on volumeCheckForPascal	ldy #$06	lda [buffPtr],y	and #$FF	cmp #$08		; is the title of the volume <= 7 chars?	bcs notPascal	cmp #$01		; is the title at least 1 char?	bcc notPascal	clc		; add 7 to length so that I can	adc #$07		; use g_volumeName as a max value for	sta temp		; the y index registerloop	iny		; check to see that the name consists	tya		; of legal chars only	cmp temp	bcs chkFileCnt	lda [buffPtr],y	and #$FFcheckDigit	cmp #$30		; is the char an ascii digit?	bcc notPascal	cmp #$3A	bcs checkUpper	bra loopcheckUpper	cmp #$41		; is the char upper case ascii?	bcc notPascal	cmp #$5b	bcs checkLower	bra loopcheckLower	cmp #$61		; is the char lower case ascii?	bcc notPascal	cmp #$7b	bcs notPascal	bra loop	chkFileCnt	ldy #io_file_count	lda [buffPtr],y	cmp #78		; are there <= 77 files in the directory?	bcc isPascalnotPascal	sec	rtsisPascal	clc	rts***************************************************************** CheckForProDOS** Return CLC if it's a ProDOS disk****************************************************************CheckForProDOS	pei <buffPtr+2	pei <buffPtr	jsr CheckProDOS2	pla	sta <buffPtr	pla	sta <buffPtr+2	;restore old buffPtr, return carry status from CheckProDOS2	rtsCheckProDOS2	lda [buffPtr]		;load backward link	bne notProDOS	ldy #$0021		;offset to minimum version	lda [buffPtr],y	and #$00FF	bne notProDOS; Now that we have checked both the backward link and version we now; need to adjust the pointer to point to the storage/name length field; within the block.	clc	lda buffPtr	adc #$0004	sta buffPtr	bcc ar	inc buffPtr+2		ar	lda [buffPtr]		;load storage/name length	tay		and #$00F0	cmp #$00F0		;is it a volume directory type?	bne notProDOS	tya	and #$000F		;isolate file name length	beq notProDOS		;must be $01 to $0F	tay;; Now we need to verify that the name is a valid ProDOS filename;ProNameLoop	lda [buffPtr],y	and #$00FF	cmp #'A'			bcc numeric	cmp #'Z'+1	bcs notProDOS	dey	bne ProNameLoop; If we get here then we need to check both the entry length and; entries per block.  If everything is OK then we will call a routine; that will build a new vcr or mark the vcr as activeits_mine	ldy #$0023-4		;index to entry length	lda [buffPtr],y	cmp #$0D27		;both entry length and entry per blk	bne notProDOS		clc		;it's a ProDOS disk	rtsnumeric	cmp #'0'			bcc period	cmp #'9'+1	bcs notProDOScontinue	dey	bne ProNameLoopnotProDOS	sec	rtsperiod	cmp #'.'			bne notProDOS	bra continue***************************************************************** CheckForISOandHS** Return: SEC if unrecognized*         CLC and X=fsid if it's High Sierra or ISO 9660****************************************************************CheckForISOandHSvol_id_end_0	equ 13	;Offset to end of 'CDROM' string.vol_id_end_1	equ 5	;Offset to end of 'CD001' string.	lda #64	sta rbBlockNum@zerotryAgain	pushlong #rbParms	pea $202f	jsl $e100b0	bcs @notHS** Ok, now look at the Volume Structure Standard Identifier.* Is it 'CDROM' (High Sierra)?*	longa off	;Set 8 bit A.	sep #$20	ldx #4	;Point to end of string.	ldy #vol_id_end_0	;Point to end of identifier.@check_hs	lda [buffPtr],y	;Get byte.	cmp hs_string,x	;Match?	bne @iso	;Nope, so not High Sierra.	dey	;Yes, done all?	dex	bpl @check_hs	;No, so loop.	rep #$30	ldx #fsid_HighSierra ;Yes, so it's High Sierra.	clc	rts** No, is it 'CD001' (ISO)?*@iso	ldx #4	;Point to end of string.	ldy #vol_id_end_1	;Point to end of identifier.@check_iso	lda [buffPtr],y	;Get byte.	cmp iso_string,x	;Match?	bne @notHS	;Nope, so not ISO either.	dey	;Yes, done all?	dex	bpl @check_iso	;No, so loop.	rep #$30	ldx #fsid_ISO9660	clc	rts@notHS	rep #$30	;added REP #$30 23-May-91 DAL	sec	rts	longa onhs_string	DC.B 'CDROM'	;Must match this for High Sierra.iso_string	DC.B 'CD001'	;Must match this for ISO.***************************************************************temp	dc.w 0	;used by ID-disk routinesrbParms	dc.w 6	;pcountrbDevNum	dc.w 0	;device numberrbAddress	dc.l 0	;buffer address	dc.l $200	;request countrbBlockNum	dc.l 0	;starting block	dc.w $200	;block size	dc.l 0	;transfer countDInfoParms	dc.w 8DInfoDevNum	dc.w 0	;device number	dc.l FormatDeviceBufferDInfoChar	dc.w 0	dc.l 0	;total blocks	dc.w 0	;slot num	dc.w 0	;unit num	dc.w 0	;versionDeviceID	dc.w 0	;dev_idFormatDeviceBuffer	dc.w 36devnameFormatDeviceName	ds.b 34***************************************************************** CheckForFST** Input: file system ID in A** Output: if FST not installed, unchanged file system ID in A*         if FST installed, A=0** This is used to prevent us from displaying a "please install* fst Blah" when they already have it installed.****************************************************************CheckForFST	sta targetFST	stz fstnum_FSTInfo@search	inc fstnum_FSTInfo	pushlong #ParBlock_FSTInfo	pea $202b	;GetFSTInfo	jsl $e100b0	bcs @notFound	lda fstID_FSTInfo	cmp targetFST	bne @search	stz targetFST@notFound	lda targetFST	rtstargetFST	dc.w 0ParBlock_FSTInfo	dc.w 2	;pCount=2fstnum_FSTInfo	dc.w 0fstID_FSTInfo	dc.w 0***************************************************************** AskWhatToDo** Input:  A = file system ID (0=could not identify)*         <dataIn = device number*         DInfo call has been made on DInfoParms block** Output: SEC if we handled the request & put a valid result*         into [dataOut],4****************************************************************AskWhatToDo	tay	beq @nothing	lda FormatDeviceName	xba	sta FormatDeviceName	pha	pha	phy	pea 12	;3 substitution strings per fsid	_Multiply	plx	pla	pha	;space for AlertWindow result	pea $0021	;button positions + Pascal sub strings	pea subTable>>16	txa	clc	adc #subTable	pha	pushlong #theMessage	_InitCursor	_AlertWindow	pla	;button number*** added 30-Apr-91 DAL	beq @zero; if they held down the Option key, turn the Init request into an Erase request	tax	lda >$e0c025	and #$0040	beq @notErase	inx@notErase	txa@zero*** end of 30-Apr-91 DAL	ldy #4	sta [<dataOut],y	sec	rts@nothing	clc	rtstheMessage	dc.b '74|The disk in device *0 appears to be in *1 format.  '	dc.b '*2'			;informational string (no FST/use Installer...)	dc.b '|^Eject|Initialize',0***************************************************************subTable	dc.l 0,0,0			;fsid_reserved	dc.l devname+1,nameProDOS,msgProDOS		;fsid_ProDOS	dc.l devname+1,nameDOS33,msgDOS33		;fsid_DOS33	dc.l 0,0,0	;devname+1,nameDOS32,msgDOS32	;fsid_DOS32	dc.l devname+1,namePascal,msgPascal		;fsid_Pascal	dc.l devname+1,nameMFS,msgMFS		;fsid_MFS	dc.l devname+1,nameHFS,msgHFS		;fsid_HFS	dc.l 0,0,0	;devname+1,nameLisa,msgLisa	;fsid_Lisa	dc.l 0,0,0	;devname+1,nameCPM,msgCPM	;fsid_CPM	dc.l 0,0,0			;fsid_reserved (9)	dc.l devname+1,nameMSDOS,msgMSDOS		;fsid_MSDOS	dc.l devname+1,nameHighSierra,msgHighSeirra	;fsid_HighSierra	dc.l devname+1,nameISO9660,msgISO9660		;fsid_ISO9660	dc.l 0,0,0	;devname+1,nameAppleShare,msgAppleShare	;fsid_AppleShare	dc.l devname+1,nameDOS33,msgDOS33other		;fakefsid_DOS33other	string pascalnameProDOS	dc.b 'ProDOS'msgProDOS	dc.b 'Installing the ProDOS File System Translator allows GS/OS to use this disk.'nameDOS33	dc.b 'Apple II DOS 3.3'msgDOS33	dc.b 'Installing ÒFile System: DOS 3.3 FSTÓ (using the Installer) allows GS/OS to read this disk.'msgDOS33other	dc.b 'The DOS 3.3 File System Translator in System 6.0.1 works only with 5.25" disks.';nameDOS32	dc.b 'Apple II DOS 3.2 or DOS 3.1';msgDOS32	dc.b 'System 6.0.1 cannot read DOS 3.2 or DOS 3.1 disks.'namePascal	dc.b 'Apple II Pascal'msgPascal	dc.b 'Installing ÒFile System: Pascal FSTÓ (using the Installer) allows GS/OS to read this disk.'nameMFS	dc.b 'Macintosh MFS'msgMFS	dc.b 'System 6.0.1 cannot read MFS disks, but it can use the newer HFS format.'nameHFS	dc.b 'HFS'msgHFS	dc.b 'Installing ÒFile System: HFS FSTÓ (using the Installer) allows GS/OS to use this disk.  HFS is used widely on the Macintosh.';nameLisa	dc.b 'Apple Lisa';msgLisa	dc.b 'System 6.0.1 cannot read Lisa disks.';nameCPM	dc.b 'CP/M';msgCPM	dc.b 'System 6.0.1 cannot read CP/M disks.'nameMSDOS	dc.b 'MS-DOS';msgMSDOS	dc.b 'An MS-DOS File System Translator is required to use this disk.'msgMSDOS	dc.b 'Installing ÒFile System: MS-DOS FSTÓ (using the Installer) allows GS/OS to read this disk.' ;9-Jun-92 DALnameHighSierra	dc.b 'High Sierra'msgISO9660msgHighSeirra	dc.b 'Installing ÒDrive: CD-ROMÓ (using the Installer) allows GS/OS to read this disk.'nameISO9660	dc.b 'ISO 9660';nameAppleShare	dc.b 'AppleShare';msgAppleShare	dc.b 'Please re-install the AppleShare software.'	string asis***************************************************************	EndP	END